---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="AI Systems Consulting – Marriott Systems"
  description="Personalised AI systems for professionals and businesses across Australia and New Zealand – Claude Code environments, custom skills, knowledge graphs, and automation workflows."
>
  <section class="consult-hero container">
    <p class="section-label" data-reveal><span aria-hidden="true">01 / </span>what we build</p>
    <div class="consult-lead-group">
      <p class="consult-lead" data-reveal>
        Marriott Systems builds personalised AI systems for professionals and business owners –
        structured setups that know your work, your clients, and how you operate. Not a chat
        window: a working layer on top of your day.
      </p>
      <p class="consult-support" data-reveal>
        In practice, that means a Claude Code environment built around you – a profile that
        persists across every session, custom shortcuts for the tasks you repeat, a knowledge
        graph that maps your documents and finds connections, and an automation roadmap for
        what to tackle next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="consult-section container">
    <p class="section-label" data-reveal><span aria-hidden="true">02 / </span>who it's for</p>
    <div class="consult-prose" data-reveal>
      <p>
        Professionals who spend too much time on work that should be faster – drafting,
        summarising, researching, preparing. Solo operators and small teams. People who have
        used AI through a browser and want something that actually knows them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Current clients include a barrister and a travel industry consultant, with engagements
        across Australia and New Zealand.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="consult-section container">
    <p class="section-label" data-reveal><span aria-hidden="true">03 / </span>how it works</p>
    <ol class="consult-steps" data-reveal>
      <li class="consult-step">
        <span class="consult-step__num mono" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <p class="consult-step__text">
          <strong class="consult-step__label">Context</strong> – before anything is built, the
          engagement starts with how you actually work: your tools, your clients, your recurring
          tasks, and the documents you keep returning to. A personalised system is only as good
          as what it knows.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="consult-step">
        <span class="consult-step__num mono" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <p class="consult-step__text">
          <strong class="consult-step__label">Build</strong> – one focused session that sets up
          the full environment: profile, rules, skills, and knowledge graph. You leave with a
          working system.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="consult-step">
        <span class="consult-step__num mono" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <p class="consult-step__text">
          <strong class="consult-step__label">Check-in</strong> – one week later, a review of
          what you have actually used, tuning what isn't working, and adding what has emerged.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="consult-step">
        <span class="consult-step__num mono" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
        <p class="consult-step__text">
          <strong class="consult-step__label">Ongoing</strong> – monthly support, new skills as
          your work evolves, graph updates, and advanced automations.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="consult-section container">
    <p class="section-label" data-reveal><span aria-hidden="true">04 / </span>flagship build</p>
    <div class="card card--lg consult-prose consult-flagship" data-reveal>
      <p>
        The fullest version of this is
        <a href="https://console.marriottsystems.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Brain Console</a>
        – a business-wide AI brain with persistent memory, tool execution, and a knowledge layer
        that centralises everything a company knows, wired into the tools it already runs on.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where a personal setup knows one professional, Brain Console knows an entire company –
        the same idea, scaled to a whole business.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="consult-section container">
    <p class="section-label" data-reveal><span aria-hidden="true">05 / </span>get in touch</p>
    <div class="card consult-prose consult-contact" data-reveal>
      <p>
        If this sounds relevant, email
        <a href="mailto:hello@marriottsystems.net">hello@marriottsystems.net</a> – a short call
        first is always fine.
      </p>
      <p>
        Running a Brisbane hospitality venue? There is a separate offer for you –
        <a href="/hospitality">websites and operational systems</a>, including a $297
        visibility audit with no call required.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ---------- Hero (section 01) ---------- */

  .consult-hero {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  /* Sticky header no longer needs the old absolute-header clearance padding –
     override the global `main > section:first-child` reset with a lighter,
     hero-appropriate top pad. Two classes needed to out-specificity that rule. */
  .consult-hero.container {
    padding-top: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 4vw, 6rem);
  }

  .consult-lead-group {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .consult-lead {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-prose);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    color: var(--text);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .consult-support {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-prose);
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  /* ---------- Standard sections (label + body grid gap; padding/border
     already come from the global `main > section` rule) ---------- */

  .consult-section {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .consult-prose {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 58ch;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-prose);
  }

  .consult-prose p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* ---------- Numbered process grid (section 03) ---------- */

  .consult-steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(1.375rem, 1.1rem + 1.3vw, 2.125rem);
  }

  .consult-step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: clamp(1rem, 0.8rem + 1vw, 1.75rem);
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .consult-step__num {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding-top: 0.3em;
  }

  .consult-step__text {
    max-width: 58ch;
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-prose);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .consult-step__label {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  /* ---------- Flagship / contact cards (sections 04–05) ---------- */

  .consult-flagship {
    max-width: none;
  }

  .consult-contact {
    max-width: none;
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .consult-lead-group,
    .consult-prose,
    .consult-steps {
      padding-left: clamp(0rem, -2rem + 10vw, 8rem);
    }
  }
</style>
